From: MOSS Windows lane <moss@example.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] install --network-open: the network, but not the cloud metadata addresses

---

Upstream: anthropics/sandbox-runtime, tag v0.0.81 (c40cf14), after 0001.
Reason: MOSS runs a command the person approved to leave the sandbox as
a pool account of its own, with every other control of the sandbox, and
the spec gives that command the network but never the cloud metadata
address. The filter set keyed to the account's user SID blocks every
connection; this adds an install mode in which that user-keyed BLOCK
matches only the metadata addresses: the link-local 169.254.0.0/16 (AWS,
GCP and Azure IMDS), Azure's WireServer 168.63.129.16, Alibaba's
100.100.100.200, Oracle's 192.0.0.192, AWS's fd00:ec2::254, and each IPv4
one in its IPv4-mapped IPv6 spelling.

Files: src/wfp.rs, src/cli.rs.

What changes, and nothing else: `install --network-open` installs the
`block-metadata` filter (user SID AND any metadata address) at each ALE
connect layer in place of `block-user`; `status` reads either as
installed. Without the flag every install is as before.

